# Authentication: use the Auth facade

Do not use the `auth()` helper. Use `Illuminate\Support\Facades\Auth` so Larastan/PHPStan can resolve the user type correctly.

```php
// ❌ Avoid — generic return type, breaks static analysis
$user = auth()->user();
if (auth()->check()) { ... }
auth()->logout();

// ✅ Prefer — Larastan infers the User model
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Auth;

$user = Auth::user();
if (Auth::check()) { ... }
Auth::logout();
```

In controllers and Form Requests with access to the request, prefer `$request->user()` when possible.
